ratorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\,x)) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\,x)) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{(\\sqrt{6}\\,x)}^{2}}\\cdot {(\\sqrt{6}\\,x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-6{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{1-6{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518158 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518063 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518158 #edb/ref 1069 "q-342834" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518158 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518158 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nCalculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}  $-\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{x{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518158 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "75d28ef3-1631-5b9b-9daa-067de055774b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518158 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nAnd the quotient rule is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}(\\frac{u}{v})}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}}\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule, chain rule, and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2})}^{′}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{({x}^{2})}^{2}}\\cdot {({x}^{2})}^{′}-\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{4}}\\cdot 2x-\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{x{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{(1-{x}^{4})\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{x{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518166 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518027 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518166 #edb/ref 1069 "q-344305" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518166 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518166 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡4{x}^{6},$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | $8{x}^{5}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518166 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7e33df1c-2868-500a-90eb-4948dc41205c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518166 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡4{x}^{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡4{x}^{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(4{x}^{6})}^{2}+1}}\\cdot {(4{x}^{6})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{12}+1}}\\cdot 24{x}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{8{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{12}+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518170 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518170 #edb/ref 1069 "q-342186" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518170 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518170 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡4{x}^{6},$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | $40{x}^{5}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518170 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "81194d8a-eb61-596d-a974-e9c1b95b27d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518170 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡4{x}^{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡4{x}^{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(4{x}^{6})}^{2}-1}}\\cdot {(4{x}^{6})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{12}-1}}\\cdot 24{x}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{40{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{12}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518178 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186517985 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518178 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96442" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518178 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518178 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nIf $y=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(3x-1),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518178 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "96d64ea4-0cd9-5375-8219-9bae598e5ccf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518178 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(3x-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(3x-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{(3x-1)}^{2}}\\cdot {(3x-1)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-(9{x}^{2}-6x+1)}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6x-9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3x(2-3x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518214 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186517986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518214 #edb/ref 1069 "q-342829" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518214 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518214 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nCalculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=7\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}\\,+$ | $7{e}^{x}\\sqrt{x}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518214 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ea0760db-381e-5949-ad3f-4c6362ce39c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518214 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nAnd the product rule is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}(u\\cdot v)}{\\text{d}x}={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule, chain rule, and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={(7\\sqrt{x})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}+7\\sqrt{x}\\cdot (\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x})^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\cdot \\text{arsinh}\\,({e}^{x})+7\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{({e}^{x})}^{2}+1}}\\cdot {({e}^{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}+7\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}+1}}\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡{e}^{x}+\\frac{7{e}^{x}\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}+1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
